{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QYGBsB47FAtG9Nzf5ARRSB","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t  \n151\t  - Vapid Keys: if you want to use solyto as a Progressive Web App with Push Notifications\n152\t  \n153\t  - BGG API Key: if you want to import games from boardgamesgeek\n154\t  \n155\t  - imgproxy keys (`imgproxy_key`, `imgproxy_salt`): if you want to use imgproxy for image processing instead of the default local processing. imgproxy is not required — solyto works out of the box without it. If you do want to use it, generate two 64-character hex strings (`openssl rand -hex 32`), write them to the secret files, and set `IMAGE_DRIVER=imgproxy` in `.env`.\n156\t  \n157\t  - TMDB Access Token (`tmdb_access_token`): if you want movie & series release notifications and trailers. Get a free Read Access Token from [themoviedb.org](https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api) after creating an account.\n158\t\n159\t**4. Configure Dev Requests (optional)**\n160\t\n161\tDev Requests is disabled by default on self-hosted instances. Submissions would stay on your local server and never reach the solyto team, which would be confusing. The feature is therefore hidden from the navigation automatically.\n162\t\n163\tIf you want to use Dev Requests as a local feedback board for your own users, set this in `.env`:\n164\t\n165\t```env\n166\tPUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS=false\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\t**5. Configure legal links (optional)**\n170\t\n171\tThe legal notice button in the navigation is hidden by default on self-hosted instances. If you want to link your users to your own imprint, privacy policy, or terms of service, set any combination of these in `.env`:\n172\t\n173\t```env\n174\tPUBLIC_LEGAL_NOTICE_URL=https://yourdomain.com/imprint\n175\tPUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://yourdomain.com/privacy\n176\tPUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://yourdomain.com/terms\n177\t```\n178\t\n179\tOnly the links you set will appear. The button stays hidden if none are set.\n180\t\n181\t**6. Configure mail (optional)**\n182\t\n183\tSet the Mailgun values in `.env` if you want outgoing email:\n184\t\n185\t```env\n186\tMAILGUN_DOMAIN=mg.yourdomain.com\n187\tMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=hello@yourdomain.com\n188\tMAIL_FROM_NAME=Solyto\n189\t```\n190\t\n191\t**7. Configure security (optional)**\n192\t\n193\tIf you want to change the default security policies, you can do so with these 3 flags:\n194\t\n195\t```env\n196\tPASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12\n197\tPASSWORD_UNCOMPROMISED=true\n198\tEMAIL_CONFIRMATION=true\n199\t```\n200\t\n201\t**8. Start**\n202\t\n203\t```sh\n204\tdocker compose up -d\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t**9. Create first user**\n208\t\n209\t```sh\n210\tdocker exec -it solyto-api so users:create\n211\t```\n212\t\n213\t*Please note: if you changed the project name via `.env`, please do also adjust the container name in this command.*\n214\t\n215\t## Networks\n216\t\n217\tThe compose file uses three networks to limit service exposure:\n218\t\n219\t- `api` — internal only, nginx and PHP talk here\n220\t- `db` — internal only, app services connect to the databases here\n221\t- `public` — externally reachable, for services that need outside connectivity\n222\t\n223\t## Storage\n224\t\n225\tThe `./storage/` directory is mounted into nginx, php, dav, and queue so they all share the same filesystem for uploads and generated files.\n226\t\n227\t## Backups\n228\t\n229\tIf you want to regularly backup your data, there are 3 components to it: the MariaDB database, the Postgres database and your local file storage containing album covers, book covers, etc.\n230\t\n231\tWe recommend using restic to automatically backup to a SFTP storage or server of your choice. Have a look at our example backup script.\n232\t\n233\t```#!/bin/bash\n234\t#!/bin/bash\n235\tset -e\n236\t\n237\tREPO=\"sftp:USER@HOST:data\"\n238\tPASSWORD_FILE=\"/etc/restic/repo.key\"\n239\tSQL_API=\"/tmp/api.sql\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06390cef-970f-4d21-9c8a-8b7a98f8b6be","uuid":"4eb9dc67-f251-4749-8b12-f33d70b04255","timestamp":"2026-10-14T17:33:01.488Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/.git/../README.md","content":"  \n  - Vapid Keys: if you want to use solyto as a Progressive Web App with Push Notifications\n  \n  - BGG API Key: if you want to import games from boardgamesgeek\n  \n  - imgproxy keys (`imgproxy_key`, `imgproxy_salt`): if you want to use imgproxy for image processing instead of the default local processing. imgproxy is not required — solyto works out of the box without it. If you do want to use it, generate two 64-character hex strings (`openssl rand -hex 32`), write them to the secret files, and set `IMAGE_DRIVER=imgproxy` in `.env`.\n  \n  - TMDB Access Token (`tmdb_access_token`): if you want movie & series release notifications and trailers. Get a free Read Access Token from [themoviedb.org](https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api) after creating an account.\n\n**4. Configure Dev Requests (optional)**\n\nDev Requests is disabled by default on self-hosted instances. Submissions would stay on your local server and never reach the solyto team, which would be confusing. The feature is therefore hidden from the navigation automatically.\n\nIf you want to use Dev Requests as a local feedback board for your own users, set this in `.env`:\n\n```env\nPUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS=false\n```\n\n**5. Configure legal links (optional)**\n\nThe legal notice button in the navigation is hidden by default on self-hosted instances. If you want to link your users to your own imprint, privacy policy, or terms of service, set any combination of these in `.env`:\n\n```env\nPUBLIC_LEGAL_NOTICE_URL=https://yourdomain.com/imprint\nPUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://yourdomain.com/privacy\nPUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://yourdomain.com/terms\n```\n\nOnly the links you set will appear. The button stays hidden if none are set.\n\n**6. Configure mail (optional)**\n\nSet the Mailgun values in `.env` if you want outgoing email:\n\n```env\nMAILGUN_DOMAIN=mg.yourdomain.com\nMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=hello@yourdomain.com\nMAIL_FROM_NAME=Solyto\n```\n\n**7. Configure security (optional)**\n\nIf you want to change the default security policies, you can do so with these 3 flags:\n\n```env\nPASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12\nPASSWORD_UNCOMPROMISED=true\nEMAIL_CONFIRMATION=true\n```\n\n**8. Start**\n\n```sh\ndocker compose up -d\n```\n\n**9. Create first user**\n\n```sh\ndocker exec -it solyto-api so users:create\n```\n\n*Please note: if you changed the project name via `.env`, please do also adjust the container name in this command.*\n\n## Networks\n\nThe compose file uses three networks to limit service exposure:\n\n- `api` — internal only, nginx and PHP talk here\n- `db` — internal only, app services connect to the databases here\n- `public` — externally reachable, for services that need outside connectivity\n\n## Storage\n\nThe `./storage/` directory is mounted into nginx, php, dav, and queue so they all share the same filesystem for uploads and generated files.\n\n## Backups\n\nIf you want to regularly backup your data, there are 3 components to it: the MariaDB database, the Postgres database and your local file storage containing album covers, book covers, etc.\n\nWe recommend using restic to automatically backup to a SFTP storage or server of your choice. Have a look at our example backup script.\n\n```#!/bin/bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -e\n\nREPO=\"sftp:USER@HOST:data\"\nPASSWORD_FILE=\"/etc/restic/repo.key\"\nSQL_API=\"/tmp/api.sql\"","numLines":90,"startLine":150,"totalLines":321}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QYGBsB47FAtG9Nzf5ARRSB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
